# Chicken Tikka Biryani Bowl

Based on [https://www.easypeasyfoodie.com/chicken-tikka-biryani/](https://www.easypeasyfoodie.com/chicken-tikka-biryani) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20251116030023/https://www.easypeasyfoodie.com/chicken-tikka-biryani/)) and [https://butfirstchai.com/chicken-tikka-biryani/](https://butfirstchai.com/chicken-tikka-biryani) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20251220044801/https://butfirstchai.com/chicken-tikka-biryani/))

{ rating="0" image="None" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

### Chicken Tikka Marinade

- [ ] 1.5 lbs [boneless chicken thighs]{ ing="boneless-chicken-thighs" }, cut into 1.5-inch pieces
- [ ] 1 cup [plain Greek yogurt]{ ing="plain-greek-yogurt" } (full-fat or 2%)
- [ ] 2 Tbsp [lemon juice]{ ing="lemon-juice" }
- [ ] 3 cloves [garlic]{ ing="garlic" }, minced
- [ ] 1 Tbsp [grated ginger]{ ing="grated-ginger" }
- [ ] 2 tsp [garam masala]{ ing="garam-masala" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [ground cumin]{ ing="ground-cumin" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [ground coriander]{ ing="ground-coriander" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [paprika]{ ing="paprika" } (or Kashmiri chili powder for color)
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [turmeric]{ ing="turmeric" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [cayenne pepper]{ ing="cayenne-pepper" } (adjust for heat)
- [ ] 1 tsp [salt]{ ing="salt" }

### Biryani Rice

- [ ] 1.5 cups [brown basmati rice]{ ing="brown-basmati-rice" }
- [ ] 2.5 cups [water or chicken broth]{ ing="water-or-chicken-broth" }
- [ ] 3 Tbsp [ghee or butter]{ ing="ghee-or-butter" }
- [ ] 1 large [onion]{ ing="onion" }, thinly sliced
- [ ] 3 cloves [garlic]{ ing="garlic" }, minced
- [ ] 1 Tbsp [grated ginger]{ ing="grated-ginger" }
- [ ] 4 [whole green cardamom pods]{ ing="whole-green-cardamom-pods" }
- [ ] 2 [bay leaves]{ ing="bay-leaves" }
- [ ] 1 [cinnamon stick]{ ing="cinnamon-stick" }
- [ ] 4 [whole cloves]{ ing="whole-cloves" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [cumin seeds]{ ing="cumin-seeds" }
- [ ] [Salt]{ ing="salt" } to taste

### Raita (Yogurt Sauce)

- [ ] 1 cup [plain Greek yogurt]{ ing="plain-greek-yogurt" }
- [ ] 1/2 [cucumber]{ ing="cucumber" }, grated and squeezed dry
- [ ] 1 Tbsp fresh [mint]{ ing="mint" }, chopped
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [cumin powder]{ ing="cumin-powder" }
- [ ] [Salt]{ ing="salt" } to taste

### Bowl Toppings

- [ ] 1/2 [red onion]{ ing="red-onion" }, thinly sliced
- [ ] 1/4 cup [white vinegar]{ ing="white-vinegar" } or lemon juice (for quick pickling)
- [ ] Fresh [cilantro]{ ing="cilantro" }, chopped
- [ ] 1/4 cup [sliced almonds]{ ing="sliced-almonds" } or cashews, toasted
- [ ] 2 [hard-boiled eggs]{ ing="hard-boiled-eggs" }, halved (optional)
- [ ] [Lemon wedges]{ ing="lemon-wedges" }

## Recipe

### Marinate the Chicken

1. In a large bowl, combine [yogurt]{ ing="plain-greek-yogurt" }, [lemon juice]{ ing="lemon-juice" }, [garlic]{ ing="garlic" }, [ginger]{ ing="grated-ginger" }, [garam masala]{ ing="garam-masala" }, [cumin]{ ing="ground-cumin" }, [coriander]{ ing="ground-coriander" }, [paprika]{ ing="paprika" }, [turmeric]{ ing="turmeric" }, cayenne, and [salt]{ ing="salt" }
1. Add chicken pieces and toss to coat thoroughly
1. Cover and refrigerate for at least 1 hour, up to 24 hours (longer = more flavor)

### Quick Pickle the Onions

1. Place sliced [red onion]{ ing="red-onion" } in a small bowl with [vinegar]{ ing="white-vinegar" } or [lemon juice]{ ing="lemon-juice" }. Let sit while preparing the rest of the dish

### Make the Biryani Rice

1. Rinse [brown basmati rice]{ ing="brown-basmati-rice" } until water runs clear. Soak in water for 20 minutes, then drain
1. In a large pot or Dutch oven, heat ghee/[butter]{ ing="ghee-or-butter" } over medium heat
1. Add sliced [onion]{ ing="red-onion" } and cook until golden brown, 8-10 minutes. Remove half of the [onions]{ ing="onion" } and set aside for garnish
1. To the remaining [onions]{ ing="onion" } in the pot, add [garlic]{ ing="garlic" }, [ginger]{ ing="grated-ginger" }, cardamom, [bay leaves]{ ing="bay-leaves" }, cinnamon, [cloves]{ ing="whole-cloves" }, and [cumin seeds]{ ing="cumin-seeds" }. Cook until fragrant, ~1 minute
1. Add drained [rice]{ ing="brown-basmati-rice" } and stir to coat with the aromatics, ~2 minutes
1. Add water/[broth]{ ing="water-or-chicken-broth" } and [salt]{ ing="salt" }. Bring to a boil, then reduce heat to low, cover, and simmer for 40-45 minutes until [rice]{ ing="brown-basmati-rice" } is tender
1. Remove from heat and let sit covered for 10 minutes. Fluff with a fork and remove whole spices if desired

### Cook the Chicken Tikka

1. Preheat oven to 425F (or heat air fryer to 400F)
1. Thread chicken pieces onto skewers if using, or arrange on a foil-lined baking sheet
1. Bake for 20-25 minutes, flipping halfway, until cooked through (internal temp 165F) and slightly charred at edges. Or air fry for 12-15 minutes, shaking halfway
1. Alternative: Cook in a hot skillet with 1 Tbsp oil over medium-high heat, 4-5 minutes per side

### Make the Raita

1. In a bowl, combine [yogurt]{ ing="plain-greek-yogurt" }, grated [cucumber]{ ing="cucumber" }, [mint]{ ing="mint" }, [cumin]{ ing="ground-cumin" }, and [salt]{ ing="salt" }. Mix well and refrigerate until serving

### Assemble Bowls

1. Divide biryani [rice]{ ing="brown-basmati-rice" } among serving bowls
1. Top with chicken tikka pieces
1. Add dollops of raita, pickled [red onions]{ ing="red-onion" }, reserved crispy [onions]{ ing="onion" }, and fresh [cilantro]{ ing="cilantro" }
1. Garnish with toasted nuts, [hard-boiled eggs]{ ing="hard-boiled-eggs" } (if using), and [lemon wedges]{ ing="lemon-wedges" }

## Notes

- **Traditional preparation:** Uses white basmati rice, which cooks in 15-20 minutes and has a lighter, fluffier texture
- **Flavor/texture tradeoff with brown rice:** Brown basmati has a chewier texture and nuttier flavor. The whole spices help add aromatic flavor to compensate. If you prefer traditional texture, use white basmati or a 50/50 white/brown blend
- **Protein alternatives:** Substitute chicken with 1.5 lbs paneer cubes, extra-firm tofu, ground turkey keema (cook with spices before adding to bowl), or a mix of chickpeas and vegetables
- **Spice level:** Adjust cayenne pepper to taste. Kashmiri chili powder gives color without much heat
- **Make ahead:** Marinate chicken up to 24 hours. Cook rice and chicken separately and store in fridge for 3-4 days. Raita lasts 2-3 days
- **Meal prep tip:** Rice reheats best with a sprinkle of water in the microwave, covered
- Related to [Chicken Tikka Masala](./chicken_tikka_masala.html) and [Butter Chicken](./butter_chicken.html)
